  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "The value $t=-3$ satisfies which of the following inequalities?\n\nI. $0\\le t-4<7$\n\nII. $t+2>-5$\n\nIII. $\\frac{t}{3}>-3$",
  "worked_solution": "We substitute the given value into each of the inequalities and check to see if the resulting statement is true or false.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=-3$ into the first inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\le t-4 & <7 \\\\ 0\\le -3-4 & <7 \\\\ 0\\le -7 & <7\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=-3$ leads to a **false** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=-3$ ** does not satisfy** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=-3$ into the second inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t+2 & >-5 \\\\ -3+2 & >-5 \\\\ -1 & >-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=-3$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=-3$ **satisfies** this inequality.\n\n- We substitute the value $t=-3$ into the third inequality. We get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{t}{3} & >-3 \\\\ \\frac{-3}{3} & >-3 \\\\ -1 & >-3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, substituting $t=-3$ leads to a **true** statement. \n\nTherefore, $t=-3$ **satisfies** this inequality.",
